			<element name="thresholdFormat" type="string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<element name="warningFormat" type="string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<element name="topFormat" type="string"/>
			<element name="leftFormat" type="string"/>
			<element name="relativeWholePeriod" type="fews:RelativePeriodComplexType" minOccurs="0"/>
			<element name="scrollableTable" type="boolean" default="false" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Use this to split the table into two parts, one for the header row(s) and one for the data rows. The data row part refers to the tableStyle for this table with "_scrollable" appended. This can be used to make the data rows scrollable while the header row(s) remain fixed. For this to work the referred style needs to be defined in the report tables .css file. This option only works if the table is written in html format.</documentation>
