			<element name="singleColumnHeader" type="string" default="Obs." minOccurs="0"/>
			<element name="suppressNameColumn" type="boolean" default="true" minOccurs="0"/>
			<element name="showWarningLevelNames" type="boolean" default="false" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>If true, then each cell in the maximumStatusTable shows the name of the warningLevel in addition to the colour of the warningLevel. If these names should be different than the names of the warningLevels, then this is possible by adding a valueAttributeMap with custom names (descriptions) and referencing the valueAttributeMap in the mapId in the timeSeries in the maximumStatusTable report configuration. Default is false.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="noThresholdsDefinedText" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>If specified, then this text is shown in cells that correspond to data for which no thresholdValueSet is defined.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="noDataAvailableText" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>If specified, then this text is shown in cells that correspond to data that has only missing values.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<sequence minOccurs="0">
				<element name="checkOnPartlyMissing" type="boolean" default="false">
					<annotation>
						<documentation>If true, then cells that correspond to data for which some (but not all) values are missing, get a different color than cells that correspond to data for which there are no missing values at all. The colour for these "partly missing" cells should be configured in the css (cascading style sheet) for the reports, as part of the element "tableStyle_thresholds_PartlyMissing", where tableStyle is the configured tableStyle for this maximumStatusTable. Default is false.</documentation>
					</annotation>
				</element>
				<element name="partlyMissingText" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType" minOccurs="0">
					<annotation>
						<documentation>If specified, then this text is shown in cells that correspond to data for which some (but not all) values are missing. Please note that this partlyMissingText is only used if checkOnPartlyMissing is true.</documentation>
					</annotation>
				</element>
			</sequence>
			<element name="scrollableTable" type="boolean" default="false" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Use this to split the table into two parts, one for the header row(s) and one for the data rows. The data row part refers to the tableStyle for this table with "_scrollable" appended. This can be used to make the data rows scrollable while the header row(s) remain fixed. For this to work the referred style needs to be defined in the report tables .css file.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
		<attribute name="id" type="fews:idStringType" use="required"/>
		<attribute name="tableStyle" type="fews:tableStyleEnumStringType" use="required"/>
