	<complexType name="FunctionRowComplexType">
		<sequence>
			<element name="header" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Text that will be displayed in the first column of the row</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="format" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Applies only to HTML tables. The format  ( colors, font, ...)  to use for this row. The available formats  for the tableStyle are defined in the report tables .css file.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="function" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>This should contain exactly one function and cannot contain any additional text or whitespace. Contains function name, variableID or tag, and optionally format id. Syntax : functionName(variableId;formatId), or  functionName(tag;formatId) Examples with variable Id: MAXVALUE(Hobs;numberFormat1),  MAXTIME(Hobs;dateFormat1). Example with a tag: ATTRIBUTE_VALUE(unit),  ATTRIBUTE_VALUE(alarmlevel; numberFormat2)</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="HtmlColumnComplexType">
		<sequence>
			<element name="thTemplate" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Since 2024.01. custom HTML for the table header.  Example 1 :  <![CDATA[<th>Location name</th>]]>>     Example 2:  <![CDATA[<th class="data-status" style="color:#F9E11E">Max value</th>]]></documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="tdTemplate" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Since 2024.01. custom HTML for the table column.  Example 1 :  <![CDATA[<td>%LOCATIONATTRIBUTE(shortname)%</td>]]>      Example 2: <![CDATA[<td class="data-status" style="color:%THRESHOLDCROSSING(MAX_THRESHOLDCOLOR;Hm)%">%THRESHOLDCROSSING(MAX_THRESHOLDNAME;Hm)%</td>]]></documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="ReportColumnComplexType">
		<sequence>
			<element name="header" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Text that will be displayed in the column header</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="format" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Applies only to HTML tables. The format  ( colors, font, ...)  to use for this column. The available formats  for the tableStyle are defined in the report tables .css file.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="width" type="positiveInteger" minOccurs="0">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Width for this column.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="FunctionColumnComplexType">
		<complexContent>
			<extension base="fews:ReportColumnComplexType">
				<sequence>
					<group ref="fews:ColorFunctionChoice" minOccurs="0">
						<annotation>
							<documentation>Since 2015.01 Applies only to HTML tables. Contains function to compute cell color. This color overrules the default color configured with element 'format'.  Examples: THRESHOLDCROSSING(MAX_THRESHOLDCOLOR;Hmeasured)   or   INDEXMAXWARNINGLEVELCOLOR(0;Hmeasured) </documentation>
						</annotation>
					</group>
					<element name="function" type="fews:nonEmptyStringType">
						<annotation>
							<documentation>Function to determine cell value. This should contain exactly one function and cannot contain any additional text or whitespace. Contains function name, variableID or tag, and optionally format id. Syntax : functionName(variableId;formatId), or  functionName(tag;formatId) Examples with variable Id: MAXVALUE(Hobs;numberFormat1),  MAXTIME(Hobs;dateFormat1). Example with a tag: ATTRIBUTE_VALUE(unit),  ATTRIBUTE_VALUE(alarmlevel; numberFormat2)</documentation>
						</annotation>
					</element>
				</sequence>
			</extension>
